  "content": {
    "title": "Tax Day food deals and freebies: White Castle, Krispy Kreme and more",
    "text": "SavorNation illustration by: Valerie Williams, SavorNation Posted: Apr 15, 2026 / 12:30 PM EDT Updated: Apr 15, 2026 / 12:30 PM EDT All the best food deals you can find on Tax Day 2026 Video Player is loading.Current Time 0:00Duration 0:29What is hangry? (SavorNation) Tax Day 2026 is here, and it’s not exactly the most exciting day of the year. Landing on April 15, it’s as reliable as Christmas without all the presents, fun, music and food. Thankfully, we found Tax Day food deals and freebies at almost a dozen chain restaurants. If you’re doing a last-minute filing, these deals may help ease the tax stress. Shake Shack releases a Masters-inspired Pimento Cheese menu We’ve hunted down deals for Tax Day 2026 at 11 national chain restaurants to help you find a place to grab a quick meal or snack so you can get back to the ol’ TurboTax before that deadline hits. They range from BOGO meals to discounts on delicious favorites, all here to ease the sting of getting those taxes done and dusted. Shipley’s Donuts Shipley’s is leaning into the 4/15 theme with their Tax Day offer of a half dozen glazed donuts for $4.15. It’s available in-store only from April 10-15, so you’ve got a few days to snag this deal. Kona Ice The mobile shaved ice franchise is offering a free Kona Ice on Tax Day (hereby renamed Chill Out Day by Kona Ice) at participating trucks. They even provide an interactive map to find out if there is one near you. Round Table Pizza Head to a Round Table Pizza location and grab 15% off orders between April 15 – 19 using the code RTP978. It’s available for valid for dine-in, carryout or delivery at participating locations. Owner of In-N-Out Burger says no to mobile ordering and pickup Fazoli’s If you’re a Rewards member, visit a participating Fazoli’s location on April 15 to grab a BOGO Baked Spaghetti deal to make sure dinner is sorted while you work through all those tax forms. Not a Rewards member yet? Just download the Fazoli’s Rewards app or sign up at their website. Great American Cookies Rewards members at Great American Cookies can make Tax Day a little sweeter with a BOGO Chocolate Chip Cookie Cake Slice deal on April 15 at participating locations (in-store only). If you aren’t already, become a rewards member by downloading the Great American Cookies Rewards app or sign up at their website. White Castle If doing taxes has you craving burgers, White Castle has you covered with 15% off your purchase using code WC15OFF between April 13-17. Smoothie King Get through those taxes by fueling up with Smoothie King. On April 15 only, the chain is offering $3 off when you join its Healthy Rewards by downloading the Smoothie King app. Pizza Hut Grab a large 3-topping pizza starting at $10 with a choice of three crusts: Hand Tossed, Tavern Style or Thin ‘N Crispy. The deal is good on April 15 only and can be claimed in-person, on the website or through the Pizza Hut app. Olive Garden Olive Garden is currently running a BOGO deal on its pasta selections. Starting at $14.99, you can buy one pasta dish for dining in and get another one free to take home with you. Sounds like a great way to eat pasta the night before those stressful taxes and then again while you’re actually doing them. Krispy Kreme On April 15 only, you can get a free dozen of Krispy Kreme’s Original Glazed donuts when you purchase any dozen donuts at regular price in the store or drive-thru. There is a limit of two free dozen per guest and those who order online can use the promo code TAXBREAK to get their free dozen. QDOBA Did you once have to pay for guac and it still haunts you? If so, it could nab you $5 off a full-sized entree at QDOBA. Just file a quick survey for your very own Tax Day Guac Relief telling the chain’s Department of Guac Affairs about your troubles. Do it by 11:59 PM ET on 4/15 to get your reward. SavorNation is reader-supported and may earn an affiliate commission.",
